<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Little movement in late trading.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Little movement in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>After-hours trading was fairly light on Monday, with few issues moving up or down from their prices at the final bell, traders said.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one volume was 113,500, compared to Friday's 158,900. Session two volume was 2,409,400, while on Friday it was 10,578,553.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
